From 7d996e64e3d922ed13d4d3dcfcb4c9c05b0ea114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:44:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Stream chat answers incrementally over server-sent events

Adds POST /api/chat/stream. Every model this app is benchmarked against streams
its answer; serving only completed responses made a deep-mode answer
indistinguishable from a hang for its entire duration, which was the most visible
behavioural gap in the parity matrix.

The stream emits grounding sources first so the UI can show provenance before the
first token, then content deltas, then one terminal event carrying timings and the
interaction id that feedback is posted against. When no model is reachable the
corpus fallback is chunked into the same event shape, so a client never branches on
which path served the answer.

Ollama is called with stream=true and read with ResponseHeadersRead so deltas
surface as they arrive rather than after the full body. Entitlement refusals travel
as an error event because the response has already committed a 200 and an SSE
content type by the time the plan is checked.

Tests: 133 passing. Coverage asserts event ordering, that concatenated deltas
reconstruct the final answer exactly, that one interaction id spans the stream and
resolves for feedback, and that an empty query yields an error event.
